// INTERNAL LINKAGE BEATS VAGUE LINKAGE (g++/clang++ canon): a file-scope
// `static` function template's instantiation and a `static inline` body
// are TU-LOCAL symbols (nm shows lowercase `t`), never weak — weak
// requires external linkage. madc used to stamp the instantiation
// vague_linkage AND internal_linkage, emitting linkonce + N_STATIC, and
// c2mir's gcc-parity check ("weak declaration of X must be public")
// walled the compile — the same collision mingw's `static __inline__`
// stdio bodies hit across the whole wine lane (75 tests, s143). Oracle:
// g++ and clang++ both compile the .cpp twin and print 42 / 10.

template <class T> static T twice(T x) { return x + x; }

static inline int half(int x) { return x / 2; }

int main()
{
    println("{}", twice(21));
    println("{}", half(20));
    return 0;
}
